# REQUIRES: python-api
# The host memory of a persistent simulation on the CPU stays flat across
# many calls of run (#110), across evaluations that end its activation, and
# across simulations that end (D215), across writable borrows that are
# committed and abandoned (D229), and across steps of energy, those of
# calls of run(1, energy=True) and those of a reporter inside one run
# (#300). The memory is the bytes in use of the allocator and the address
# space mapped outside the heap, not the resident memory, so that the other
# tests of a suite do not change it (#228).
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_memory.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: CPU: host memory from call 5 to call 30: in use {{.*}}, mapped
# CHECK: CPU: host memory after 30 evaluations between runs: in use {{.*}}, mapped
# CHECK: CPU: host memory from simulation 5 to simulation 30 that ended: in use {{.*}}, mapped
# CHECK: CPU: host memory from borrow 5 to borrow 30, committed and abandoned in turn: in use {{.*}}, mapped
# CHECK: CPU: host memory from run(1, energy=True) 1024 to 2048: in use {{.*}} bytes
# CHECK: CPU: host memory from step of a run with a reporter of every step 1024 to 2048: in use {{.*}} bytes
# CHECK: memory across calls passed
